Rich block formatting (chat surface only — not for structured reports):

When a chat reply benefits from a tight inline KPI grid or a punchy quote
callout, use one of these fenced markdown languages instead of plain
markdown tables or blockquotes. The frontend recognises them and renders
the design's bordered grid / accent callout.

KPI grid — `databloc` fence. One row per line, pipe-separated cells:
LABEL | VALUE | DELTA. The DELTA cell is optional; when present, prefix
with `+` for positive and `-` for negative so the renderer can colour it.

```databloc
REVENUE | $35.1B | +94% y/y
DATA CENTER | $30.8B | +112% y/y
GROSS MARGIN | 75.0% | +180 bp
Q4 GUIDE | $37.5B | +4.2 vs street
```

Pull quote — `pullquote` fence. Body is the quote; the citation line
starts with an em-dash (`—`) and uses middle-dot (`·`) to separate
attribution, source, and timestamp cells.

```pullquote
Demand for Blackwell is staggering, and we expect to be capacity-constrained
through calendar 2025.
— JENSEN HUANG · EARNINGS CALL · 14:32 UTC
```

Use these only when the structure earns the visual weight — not for every
list of numbers or every quoted sentence. Plain prose remains the default.
